{
  "dom_id": "questionExplanation-1275",
  "name": null,
  "problem": "",
  "worked_solution": "A partition of a set $Y$ is a collection of non-empty subsets of $Y$ where every element of $Y$ is contained in *exactly* one subset. \n\nOf the given collections, only $\\{\\{2,4,6,…,40\\},\\{42,44,46,…,60\\},\\{62,64,66,…,100\\}\\}$ is a partition.\n\nThe rest of the collections are not partitions:\n\n- $\\{\\{2,4,6,…,40\\},\\{80,82,84,…,100\\}\\}$ is not a partition because many elements of $Y$ (such as $42$) do not appear in any subsets.\n\n- $\\{\\{2,4,6,…,40\\},\\{20,22,24,…,100\\}\\}$ is not a partition because many elements (such as $20$) appear in both subsets.\n\n- $\\{\\{1,2,3,…,100\\}\\}$ is not a partition because it contains many elements (such as $1$) that do not appear in $Y.$\n\n- $\\{\\{4,6,8,10\\},\\{10,11,12,…,100\\}\\}$ is not a partition because it contains many elements (such as $11$) that do not appear in $Y.$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
  "fields": [],
  "problem_field_keys": [],
  "answer_fields_complete": null,
  "result": null,
  "proof_feedback": null,
